{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"6 frames created: 01_Dashboard 10:2, 02_Timeline 10:3, 03_Task_Board 10:4, 04_Files 10:5, 05_Settings 10:6, 06_Messages 10:7. DM Sans has all styles including SemiBold and Bold.\n\nNow build components — part A: Top Bar, Nav Rail (6 variants with reactions), Tags (4 variants), Icon Button, Chat Bubbles.\n\nNav rail reactions: destinations:\n- Dashboard → 10:2, Timeline → 10:3, Task → 10:4, Files → 10:5, Settings → 10:6, Messages → 10:7.\n\nReaction format: try `{action:{type:'NODE',destinationId:id,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:null,preserveState:false}, trigger:{type:'CLICK'}}`. If error, try minimal.\n\nComponents placement: components area at y=1250+. Top Bar at (0,1250). Rails at (1450,1250) spaced 140. Tags at (1450+6*140=2290, 1250) spaced 120. Icon buttons row below? I'll lay out:\n- Top Bar: (0,1250)\n- Rails: x = 1500 + i*140, y=1250\n- Tags: x=1500, y=2320, spaced 110\n- Icon Button: x=1500+4*110+40? Put at (1500,2400)... let me: Tags row y=2350 x=1500..; Icon Button at (1500, 2410)? Rails are 1024 tall so tags go at y=1250+1024+60=2334. Icon Button at x=1500+5*110, y=2334. Bubbles below at y=2410.\n\nFine — positioning doesn't need to be beautiful, but reasonably organized.\n\nCode for call 2:\n\n```js\nconst page=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('8:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nawait Promise.all(['Regular','Medium','SemiBold','Bold'].map(s=>figma.loadFontAsync({family:'DM Sans',style:s})));\n// helpers\nconst hex=..., solid=...\nfunction txt(...)\nfunction frame(...)\nasync function icon(id,size,color){const c=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);const i=c.createInstance();if(size&&size!==24)i.resize(size,size);if(color)recolor(i,color);return i;}\nfunction recolor(node,h){const s=solid(h);const walk=n=>{if('fills' in n&&Array.isArray(n.fills)&&n.fills.length&&n.fills[0].type==='SOLID')n.fills=[s];if('strokes' in n&&Array.isArray(n.strokes)&&n.strokes.length&&n.strokes[0].type==='SOLID')n.strokes=[s];if('children' in n)n.children.forEach(walk);};walk(node);}\n```\n\nWait — recolor replacing strokes color keeps weight. But careful: for icons that use strokes, strokes=[s] preserves strokeWeight. OK.\n\nNav button:\n```js\nfunction navBtn(iconCompId, current){\n  const b=figma.createFrame(); b.resize(48,48); b.cornerRadius=14;\n  b.fills=[current?solid('EDEDFE'):solid('FFFFFF',0)];\n  b.layoutMode='HORIZONTAL'; b.primaryAxisAlignItems='CENTER'; b.counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER';\n  const ic=iconSync... // need async\n}\n```\nSince icon creation is async, I'll make navBtn async.\n\nTop bar: build absolute:\n```js\nconst tb=figma.createComponent? \n```\nHmm — for TopBar and others I want COMPONENT nodes: figma.createComponent(); c.resizeWithoutConstraints(w,h)... createComponent returns component 100×100 default; resize it.\n\nTopBar:\n```js\nconst tb=figma.createComponent(); tb.name='Top Bar'; tb.resize(1352,80); tb.x=0; tb.y=1250; tb.fills=[solid('FFFFFF')]; tb.strokes=[solid('E8E9F0')]; tb.strokeBottomWeight? \n```\nIndividual stroke weights: strokeTopWeight etc. supported on frames (individual strokes). Use tb.strokeBottomWeight=1 with strokes set and others 0: set strokeWeight=0 then strokeBottomWeight=1. Actually setting individual weights: tb.strokeTopWeight=0 etc. Works when strokes non-empty.\n\nSearch: frame 440×44 bg F4F5F9 radius 22 at (24,18). Icon Search 20 recolored 8C8C9E at (18,12). Text at (48,13) \"Search anything...\" 14 Regular 8C8C9E. Vertically center text: h 44, text ~18 → y=13.\n\nBell: 44×44 at (1208,18), bg F4F5F9 radius 12? make circle? Use rounded 12. Icon_Bell 20 ink at center. Badge: 16×16 circle EB5757 at (1238,14) with \"2\" 10 Medium white centered — badge needs text centered: frame 16×16 radius 8 AL center, text 10.\n\nWait badge should be brand or red? \"notifications with count 2\" — badge red is conventional. Use brand #5051F9? I'll use brand to keep palette tight... Red draws attention; choose red EB5757? Hmm — my palette includes red for tags. Notification badge red is standard. Use EB5757.\n\nAvatar: 40×40 at (1264,20) radius 20. Chevron 16 at (1312,32) recolored 6E7191.\n\nPositions: tb width 1352; right padding 24: chevron at x=1352-24-16=1312. avatar 1264 (1312-8-40). bell 1208 (1264-16-44). \n\nRails:\n```js\nconst navDefs=[['Dashboard','6:25','10:2'],['Timeline','6:30','10:3'],['Task','6:29','10:4'],['Settings','6:28','10:6'],['Messages','6:27','10:7'],['Files','6:26','10:5']];\nasync function makeRail(current){\n  const c=figma.createComponent(); c.name='Nav Rail / '+current; c.resize(88,1024); c.fills=[solid('FFFFFF')]; c.strokes=[solid('E8E9F0')]; c.strokeWeight=0; c.strokeRightWeight=1;\n  const logo=await comp(6:39)... place x=28.5,y=28 (w31,h36)\n  wordmark 'OCTOM.' 14 Bold ink, width 88 center at y=72.\n  icons start y=132 step 60.\n  for each def: btn 48×48 at x=20; AL center; icon 24 (recolor: current? brand : sub); name button node; set reactions on btn: link to dest.\n  return c;\n}\nfor i in 0..5: makeRail(navDefs[i][0]) at x=1500+i*140, y=1250.\n```\nReaction: btn.reactions=[{action:{type:'NODE',destinationId:dest,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:null,preserveState:false},trigger:{type:'CLICK'}}]. Test — if throws, catch and try without extra fields.\n\nTags:\n```js\nconst tagDefs=[['Design','5051F9','EDEDFE'],['Research','12A594','E0F5F2'],['Planning','F79009','FEF0E0'],['Content','EB5757','FDEAEA']];\nfunction makeTag(name,fg,bg){const c=figma.createComponent();c.name='Tag / '+name;c.layoutMode='HORIZONTAL';c.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO';c.counterAxisSizingMode='AUTO';c.paddingLeft=10;c.paddingRight=10;c.paddingTop=4;c.paddingBottom=4;c.cornerRadius=999;c.fills=[solid(bg)];const t=txt(name,11,'Medium',fg);t.name='Label';c.appendChild(t);c.x=...;return c;}\n```\nNote: for AL component sizing AUTO, need to set after layoutMode. Set c.x/c.y after.\n\nIcon Button:\n```js\nconst ib=figma.createComponent(); ib.name='Icon Button'; ib.resize(40,40); ib.cornerRadius=12; ib.fills=[solid('F4F5F9')]; ib.layoutMode='HORIZONTAL'; ib.primaryAxisAlignItems='CENTER'; ib.counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER'; ib.primaryAxisSizingMode='FIXED'; ib.counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED';\nconst ic=await icon('6:33',20,'14142B'); ic.name='Icon'; ib.appendChild(ic);\n```\nCareful: setting layoutMode after resize keeps size. Child icon 20×20. When swapping later, new icon should be resized 20.\n\nBubbles:\n```js\nfunction makeBubble(kind){const c=figma.createComponent();c.name='Chat Bubble / '+kind;c.layoutMode='HORIZONTAL';c.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO';c.counterAxisSizingMode='AUTO';c.paddingLeft=14;c.paddingRight=14;c.paddingTop=10;c.paddingBottom=10;c.cornerRadius=14;c.maxWidth=340;\nif(kind==='In'){c.fills=[solid('FFFFFF')];c.strokes=[solid('E8E9F0')];c.strokeWeight=1;c.topLeftRadius=4;}else{c.fills=[solid('5051F9')];c.topRightRadius=4;}\nconst t=txt(kind==='In'?'Message text':'Your message',13,'Regular',kind==='In'?'14142B':'FFFFFF');t.name='Text';c.appendChild(t);return c;}\n```\nmaxWidth property on frames: 'maxWidth' exists. OK.\n\nNames for text children so overrides are easy: 'Text', 'Label', etc.\n\nComponent naming for instance lookup: I'll return all IDs from the call.\n\nLet me now write call 2 fully. Keep under 50k chars — fine.\n\nOne thing: figma.createComponent() then setting layoutMode with AUTO sizing: must set primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO' and counterAxisSizingMode='AUTO' then paddings; the component auto-sizes after appendChild.\n\nFor nav rails, the reaction: I need try/catch to find accepted shape. I'll attempt full shape; on exception, log fallback attempt. I'll write:\n\n```js\nfunction link(node,dest){ try{ node.reactions=[{action:{type:'NODE',destinationId:dest,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:null,preserveState:false},trigger:{type:'CLICK'}}]; } catch(e){ node.reactions=[{action:{type:'NODE',destinationId:dest},trigger:{type:'CLICK'}}]; } }\n```\n\nAlso — creating 6 rails × 6 icons = 36 async icon instances; ea