{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found it. The reactions format is wrong:\n- trigger type must be 'ON_CLICK' not 'CLICK'\n- action must NOT include 'preserveState' (unrecognized key)\n\nCorrect format: `{action:{type:'NODE',destinationId:'10:2',navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:null},trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}}`\n\nThat's why my original script failed — but wait, my original `link()` had try/catch... The catch would have caught this and tried the fallback `{action:{type:'NODE',destinationId:dest},trigger:{type:'CLICK'}}` — which would ALSO throw (trigger 'CLICK' invalid), and THAT throw propagated out of the catch block! That's the bug. The error at line 26:39 was the throw inside the catch of link() during the nav rails section.\n\nNow fix: link = reactions=[{action:{type:'NODE',destinationId:dest,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:null},trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}}].\n\nLet me verify quickly within the next main call — I'll just use this format directly; if it fails, the call errors and I'll see it.\n\nNow re-run the full component build with corrected link().","signature":"d8402664bf9849888a1ea20e"}],"id":"ccff3541-4cbe-4bf0-a121-232c26643398","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0440d75-2a96-47fc-b3b2-8ce028ebb095","uuid":"d08b48d9-d0f2-4a5b-b625-97dffc3192e4","timestamp":"2026-11-01T23:41:54.573Z","thinking_duration_ms":5165}
