rrors, try without. Actually to minimize retries, maybe I should test the reaction format FIRST in a tiny probe... but that costs a call. Alternative: wrap link() in try/catch with two formats: first `actions:[...]`, on error fall back to `action:...`. Log which worked. That's robust — single call.\n\nLet me write:\n\n```js\nfunction link(node,dest){\n  try{\n    node.reactions=[{actions:[{type:'NODE',destinationId:dest,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:null}],trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}}];\n    log.push('link actions ok');\n  }catch(e){\n    node.reactions=[{action:{type:'NODE',destinationId:dest,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:null},trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}}];\n    log.push('link action fallback: '+e.message);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nGood. Everything else same as before.","signature":"7bf6c401cf75477eb60390c8"}],"id":"5b83dace-b44c-40d5-a788-65795bb1d5f0","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0440d75-2a96-47fc-b3b2-8ce028ebb095","uuid":"f87e937f-5e8f-4b60-b206-cff9b8d5bce5","timestamp":"2026-11-01T23:50:54.816Z","thinking_duration_ms":12827}
