{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a full product design benchmark in the assigned Figma file https://www.figma.com/design/b6HOXVpSd1U75KpjQDhJ6b/ (fileKey b6HOXVpSd1U75KpjQDhJ6b). Requirements:\n   - Confirm assigned account via whoami: zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai (CONFIRMED in earlier session)\n   - Read \"00 · Start Here\" for product/screens/states/data/copy/prototype requirements; read \"01 · Foundations\" for visual rules; reuse \"02 · Components\"; use \"04 · Media\" assets; deliver complete design into \"03 · Workspace\" (page 8:2)\n   - Preserve all reference pages and their nodes; do not replace them, create a different Figma file, or switch accounts/teams. Starter instructions about read-only sources apply to reference pages, NOT the workspace\n   - Build exactly 6 frames named exactly: 01_Dashboard, 02_Timeline, 03_Task_Board, 04_Files, 05_Settings, 06_Messages (1440×1024, light mode, desktop web) + reusable components + clickable prototype\n   - Copy/data must match \"Fixed data\" verbatim; brand color #5051F9 and DM Sans are fixed; other colors are mine to define\n   - Use whoami → get_metadata → read-only use_figma → use_figma build → get_screenshot; inspect screenshots of ALL screens, fix visible problems, re-verify; screenshot success alone is not completion\n   - Use tools directly without delegating to other agents; load fonts before text edits; build in manageable sections; add prototype interactions after screens exist\n   - Unattended session: resolve routine choices autonomously using the brief; report real limitations if blocked\n   - Protocol: every assistant message before a tool call must start with \"Reasoning summary:\"; after each tool result do the same before the next call; final response first line \"Reasoning summary: ...\" then \"Final answer:\" with assigned file URL, 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations\n   - MUST NEVER use loadAllPagesAsync, setPluginData, createImageAsync; must use `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page)`\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via mcp__figma__use_figma; state does NOT persist between calls — all helpers re-declared each call\n   - **Reactions format (VALIDATED)**: `node.reactions=[{actions:[{type:'NODE',destinationId:dest,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:null}],trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}}]` — `actions` is an ARRAY; trigger 'ON_CLICK'; component-level reactions on nav buttons inside Nav Rail components are inherited by all instances\n   - **Component IDs must be resolved**: `comps[k]=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('6:39')` — string IDs cause \"TypeError: not a function\" on `.createInstance()`\n   - **No Bash/Read/Write tools in this environment** — only 4 Figma MCP tools exist (get_metadata, get_screenshot, use_figma, whoami); screenshots must be viewed with `enableBase64Response:true` (inline base64 image) since curl download is impossible\n   - get_screenshot can time out at 120s — direct retry works\n   - Failed use_figma calls roll back atomically; per-statement try/catch allows partial commits + error localization\n   - **Node identification by unique properties** (width, fontSize, characters) — beware first-match collisions when multiple nodes share characters (e.g., three '10:30 AM' texts); use unique discriminators like resized width===476\n   - `textAutoResize='WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT'` can be set post-hoc to collapse a resized right-aligned text box to natural width\n   - Vector normalization probe (vnorm) pattern for polyline positioning; `let px=0,py=0` declared before poly() uses them\n   - DM Sans styles: 'Regular','Medium','SemiBold','Bold' (all loadable)\n   - figma.createText() auto-adds to currentPage — un-appended nodes become stray page children\n   - dashPattern property for dashed upload-zone borders\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Figma file b6HOXVpSd1U75KpjQDhJ6b, page 8:2 (03 · Workspace)** — only writable target\n   - **Components (created earlier, all on page 8:2)**: Top Bar 16:6; Nav Rails: Dashboard 18:13, Timeline 18:48, Task 18:83, Settings 18:118, Messages 18:153, Files 18:188 (each has 6 nav buttons with component-level ON_CLICK reactions → 10:2/10:3/10:4/10:6/10:7/10:5 — VERIFIED); Tags: Design 16:26, Research 16:28, Planning 16:30, Content 16:32; Icon Button 16:34; Chat Bubble/In 16:37, Chat Bubble/Out 16:39; Gradients: Blue 6:50, Glass 6:51, Orange 6:52, Red 6:53; Photos: Chat_Design_1 6:48, Chat_Design_2 6:49\n   - **Icon component IDs**: dashboard 6:25, files 6:26, messages 6:27, settings 6:28, task 6:29, timeline 6:30, arrow-up 6:5, attachment 6:6, bell 6:7, calendar 6:8, checklist 6:9, chevron-down 6:10, chevron-left 6:11, chevron-right 6:12, clock 6:13, comment 6:14, emoji 6:15, file 6:16, folder 6:17, grid 6:18, image 6:19, link 6:20, mail 6:21, mic 6:22, more 6:23, more-v 6:24, phone 6:31, play 6:32, plus 6:33, search 6:34, send 6:35, upload 6:36, upload-cloud 6:37, video 6:38\n   - **Avatar component IDs**: cris 6:42, charmie 6:55, jason 6:44, charlie 6:40, user 6:43, team 6:58, killan 6:45, claudia 6:41, novita 6:47, milie 6:46, ikhsan 6:56, aditya 6:54, ahmed 6:57\n   - **Screens built this session**:\n     - **03_Task_Board (10:4)** — DONE (39 children): rail 18:83 + topbar; header \"🔥 Task\" (112,108) + avatars aditya/charmie/novita/milie 32px (1218..1284) + \"+6\" circle (1308) + 44×44 brand plus button (1372,104); 4 columns at x=112/348/584/820 w=220 (dots: Backlog 8C8C9E, To Do 1DA7FF, In Progress F79009, Review 2BB673; count chip \"3\"; plus icon); 12 cards (cover h=182, no-cover h=110, w=220 r12): Backlog: Design/Create s